<!--
  A question put before something is done that the person may not mean, over the window
  while it is asked. Revert's was the first (spec/06-library.md, rule 12a):

      Revert "the song's name" to how it was when it was opened?
      This takes back EVERY change made to this song since it was opened in this
      editor.
                                        [ Revert All Changes ]  [ Cancel ]

  and the two that putting a copy's chords into its original asks are the others
  (spec/08-repair.md, D; LibraryModel.Folding.cs): what is about to be done, before it
  is; and, after, whether the copy is to be moved out of the library.

  The second button, Cancel or what the question names it, is what Esc and Enter give:
  Enter is not to be what throws an hour's work away, or takes a file out of a library.
  A click on the dimmed window behind gives it too.

  It is drawn in the window, as the earlier versions are, and is not a window of the
  system's: the system's own asks with buttons it names itself, Yes or OK, and these
  buttons are to say what they do. The words are LibraryModel's.
-->
<UserControl x:Class="Pro7ChordEditor.AppViews.QuestionPanel"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             KeyboardNavigation.TabNavigation="Cycle"
             KeyboardNavigation.DirectionalNavigation="Cycle">
  <Grid>
    <Border Background="#73000000" MouseLeftButtonDown="OutsideWasClicked" />
    <Border MaxWidth="470"
            HorizontalAlignment="Center"
            VerticalAlignment="Center"
            Margin="36"
            CornerRadius="8"
            BorderThickness="1"
            BorderBrush="{DynamicResource DividerStrokeColorDefaultBrush}"
            Background="{DynamicResource ApplicationBackgroundBrush}">
      <StackPanel Margin="20,18,20,16">
        <TextBlock x:Name="Heading" FontSize="15" FontWeight="SemiBold" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
        <TextBlock x:Name="Message" Margin="0,10,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Margin="0,18,0,0">
          <Button x:Name="Yes" Click="YesWasClicked" />
          <Button x:Name="Cancel" Margin="8,0,0,0" IsDefault="True" IsCancel="True" Click="CancelWasClicked" />
        </StackPanel>
      </StackPanel>
    </Border>
  </Grid>
</UserControl>
